==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|nautical|lang=en}} The [[top]] of a [[mast]].
#*'''1851''', [[w:Herman Melville|Herman Melville]], ''[[w:Moby Dick|Moby Dick]]'', [[s:Moby-Dick/Chapter 35|chapter 35]]
#*:In most American whalemen the '''mast-heads''' are manned almost simultaneously with the vessel’s leaving her port; even though she may have fifteen thousand miles, and more, to sail ere reaching her proper cruising ground. 
# {{context|US|lang=en}} A [[list]] of a [[newspaper]] or other [[periodical]]'s main [[staff]], contributing [[writer]]s, [[publisher]], [[circulation]], [[advertising]] [[rate]]s etc.
# {{context|UK|lang=en}} The [[title]] (normally in a large and distinctive [[font]]) of a [[newspaper]] at the top of the [[front page]]

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|nautical|transitive|lang=en}} To send to the masthead as a [[punishment]].
#: {{rfquotek|Marryat}}
#* '''2009''', Gregory Fremont-Barnes, ''Nelson's Officers and Midshipmen'' (page 30)
#*: When the ship happened to be in a warm climate, '''mastheading''' constituted a fairly mild punishment; indeed, many regarded it as rather a relief from duty. But in inclement weather the experience was most unpleasant.

